#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# quotient

#% text
# `quotient(a, b)` gives the integer quotient `floor(a/b)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The quotient rounds towards `-inf`, so that `a == b*quotient(a, b) + mod(a, b)` with `mod(a, b)` of the sign of `b`.

#% item
# Integers, rationals and machine numbers are accepted; symbolic arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# `quotient` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
quotient(17, 5)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
quotient(-17, 5)
#% output
#= -4

#% cell
quotient(17, -5)
#% output
#= -4

#% cell
quotient(7.5, 2)
#% output
#= 3

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Large integers:

#% cell
quotient(10^30, 7)
#% output
#= 142857142857142857142857142857

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
quotient([10, 11, 12, 13], 4)
#% output
#= [2, 2, 3, 3]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The division identity:

#% cell
a = -23; b = 6; b*quotient(a, b) + mod(a, b)
#% output
#= -23

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `mod`, `quotient_remainder`, `floor`, `gcd`
